module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.ConeSituation
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaReflector
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The triangulated structure of `K(Mod^dg(C))`, as instances

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R`. Axioms (A), (B) and (C)
for the differential graded category `Mod^dg(C)` of right differential graded `C`-modules are
assembled in `DGCategory.rightModuleConeSituation`, and
`DGCategory.homotopyCategory_isTriangulated` turns a `DGCategory.ConeSituation` into a
triangulated structure on the homotopy category. Both are stated with `letI`, because a
`ConeSituation` is a hypothesis bundle rather than a typeclass and the generic file cannot
know which bundle a reader means. For `Mod^dg(C)` there is only one bundle, so here the
structures are registered as instances and the triangulatedness of `K(Mod^dg(C))` becomes
automatic.

With them in scope, step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for the localizing subcategory generated by a
family of representables holds for every differential graded category, with no hypothesis
beyond the differential graded category itself and the family.

## Main definitions

* `DGCategory.hasShiftRightModuleHomotopyCategory`: the translation functors of axiom (B).
* `DGCategory.pretriangulatedRightModuleHomotopyCategory`: the pretriangulated structure whose
  distinguished triangles are those of admissible short exact sequences.

## Main results

* `DGCategory.isTriangulatedRightModuleHomotopyCategory`: `K(Mod^dg(C))` is triangulated.
* `DGCategory.shiftFunctor_rightModuleHomotopyCategory` and
  `DGCategory.distinguishedTriangles_rightModuleHomotopyCategory`: what the two instances
  carrying data are, read off the registered instances rather than the `letI` ones.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`: step 1 of
  [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for a family of representables, with no triangulatedness hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The preadditive structure is already an instance, as
`DGCategory.preadditiveRightModuleHomotopyCategory`; the five registered here are the
remaining ones that `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated` and `CategoryTheory.IsTriangulated` ask
for. Each is the term the corresponding `letI` of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.HomotopyCategoryTriangulated` installs, applied
to `DGCategory.rightModuleConeSituation`, so the statements proved there about the `letI`
structures are statements about these instances. Nothing else in the development puts a
shift, a zero object or a pretriangulated structure on `DGCategory.K`, so no second structure
competes with them: the two pretriangulated structures that do compete on a homotopy category
in this development, `DifferentialGradedModule.instPretriangulatedHomotopyCategory` and
`DifferentialGradedModule.instPretriangulatedHomotopyCategory'`, live on the homotopy category
of the differential graded modules over a differential graded algebra, which is a different
category.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09QY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09QY)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DGCategory

universe w v u r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] {C : DGCategory.{v, u} R}

/-- The translation functors of `K(Mod^dg(C))` are those of axiom (B) for `Mod^dg(C)`. -/
@[sga "4½ Etat_0 1.2.2" "special case"]
noncomputable instance hasShiftRightModuleHomotopyCategory :
    HasShift (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K ℤ :=
  (rightModuleShiftAxiomB.{w} C).kShift

/-- The zero right differential graded module is a zero object of `K(Mod^dg(C))`. -/
instance hasZeroObjectRightModuleHomotopyCategory :
    HasZeroObject (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K :=
  homotopyHasZeroObject _ (rightModuleConeSituation.{w} C)

/-- Each translation functor of `K(Mod^dg(C))` is additive. -/
@[sga "4½ Etat_0 1.2.2" "special case"]
instance shiftFunctorAdditiveRightModuleHomotopyCategory (n : ℤ) :
    (shiftFunctor (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K n).Additive :=
  homotopyShiftAdditive _ (rightModuleConeSituation.{w} C) n

/-- `K(Mod^dg(C))` is pretriangulated, its distinguished triangles being those isomorphic to
the triangle of an admissible short exact sequence of right differential graded modules. -/
@[sga "4½ Etat_0 1.2.2" "special case"]
noncomputable instance pretriangulatedRightModuleHomotopyCategory :
    Pretriangulated (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K :=
  homotopyPretriangulated _ (rightModuleConeSituation.{w} C)

/-- `K(Mod^dg(C))` is triangulated. -/
instance isTriangulatedRightModuleHomotopyCategory :
    IsTriangulated (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K :=
  rightModuleHomotopyCategory_isTriangulated.{w} C

/-- The translation functor `⟦1⟧` of `K(Mod^dg(C))` is the shift functor of axiom (B) on the
homotopy category. -/
theorem shiftFunctor_rightModuleHomotopyCategory (n : ℤ) :
    shiftFunctor (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K n =
      ((rightModuleShiftAxiomB.{w} C).shiftFunctor n).onK :=
  (rightModuleShiftAxiomB.{w} C).kShift_functor n

/-- The distinguished triangles of `K(Mod^dg(C))` are exactly the triangles isomorphic to that
of an admissible short exact sequence of right differential graded modules. -/
theorem distinguishedTriangles_rightModuleHomotopyCategory :
    distinguishedTriangles (C := (rightModuleCategory.{w} C).K) =
      {U | IsDistinguishedTriangle _ (rightModuleConeSituation.{w} C) U} :=
  distinguishedTriangles_homotopyPretriangulated _ (rightModuleConeSituation.{w} C)

namespace RightModule

/-- **Step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] for a family of representable right differential graded
modules, unconditionally.** Let `C` be a differential graded category whose objects and whose
morphism modules live in one universe, and let `G` be a family of objects of `C` indexed by
that universe. Let `N` be the localizing subcategory of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the
representables `h_{G i} = C(-, G i)`. Then there is an exact functor `L` of `K(Mod^dg(C))` and
a unit `η : 𝟭 ⟶ L` such that every `L X` is local, `η` is universal among morphisms into a
local object, and the cone of `η` lies in `N`.

This is `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK` with its
triangulatedness hypotheses discharged by the instances of this file, which come from axioms
(A), (B) and (C) for `Mod^dg(C)`. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R)
    {ι : Type v} (G : ι → C.Obj) :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated) (η : 𝟭 _ ⟶ L),
      (∀ X, (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal (L.obj X)) ∧
      (∀ Y, (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.rightOrthogonal Y →
        ∀ X, Function.Bijective fun φ : L.obj X ⟶ Y => η.app X ≫ φ) ∧
      (∀ (X Z) (f : Z ⟶ X) (g : L.obj X ⟶ Z⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
        Triangle.mk f (η.app X) g ∈ distTriang _ →
          (ofObj fun i => yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v} Z) :=
  exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK C G

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
